During this assignment, I wrote a program where every time you press a button on the Arduino, it randomly lights up a different colored LED. The LED stays on as long as you have the button pressed, and turns off when you let go.  I started by defining variables for the four different colored LEDs and the button, and then setup the LEDs to receive output while the button sent input. 

To complete this assignment more efficiently, I'd tell my past self to:
1. begin with defining my variables and their functions
2. define those variables as either inputs or outputs
2. sketch out the process I need to repeat in my loop code
